sequenceDiagram
    actor R as Student (rider)
    participant SC as :Schedule Screen
    participant SM as :Schedule Manager
    participant RS as :RecurringSchedule (rider)
    participant SL as :ScheduleSlot
    participant DS as :RecurringSchedule (driver)
    participant PM as :Potential Match
    participant MS as :Match Results Screen

    Note over R,MS: Step 6 - Validate and save the rider's recurring schedule
    R->>SC: (5) save recurring schedule (days and times)
    SC->>SM: 6.1 send selected days and times
    SM->>RS: 6.2 validate days and times are complete
    RS-->>SM: valid (or missing information)
    SM->>RS: 6.3 store recurring schedule owned by the rider
    SM->>SL: 6.4 store one schedule slot per selected day and time
    SM->>SC: 6.5 display save confirmation

    Note over R,MS: Step 8 - Compare rider needs with driver schedules
    R->>SC: (7) select "find compatible schedules"
    SC->>SM: 8.1 request compatible matches
    SM->>SL: 8.2 retrieve the rider's schedule slots
    SL-->>SM: rider's days and times
    SM->>DS: 8.3 find driver schedules with slots sharing a day and overlapping times
    DS-->>SM: compatible driver schedules (may be none)
    SM->>PM: 8.4 create potential matches (day, times, driver)
    SM->>MS: 8.5 display potential matches (or "no compatible schedules")

    Note over R,MS: Step 10 - Show the selected driver's ride information
    R->>MS: (9) select a potential driver
    MS->>SM: 10.1 request selected driver's ride information
    SM->>PM: 10.2 retrieve selected match
    SM->>DS: 10.3 retrieve the driver's schedule and slots
    SM->>MS: 10.4 display driver ride information and option to coordinate (UC-05)
